## D4-disk. Growth projection inputs
- /var/lib/dg = 6.2 MB during drills (8 drill DBs + 09-21 residue, pre-purge).
  Drill DBs: ~16–98 KiB each (fleet imports 16–24 KiB, 40k-row burst 98 KiB).
  Disk headroom enormous (25 GiB free); no quota needed at this scale.
  Transfer staging worst case stays ≤ 8 x 128 MiB TTL'd per design.

## Method incident (no service fault)
- First three soak attempts "stalled" ~60 s: the driver opened a fresh TCP
  connection per request (~250/s) and exhausted loopback ephemeral ports
  (4096 TIME-WAIT observed, SYN-SENT pile-up). Service was never wedged
  (canary 200 throughout, idle host, clean journal). Fixed with keep-alive
  connections; 600 s + 300 s runs then completed. Lesson: drill drivers must
  reuse connections; a future `dg bench` subcommand should own this.

